WEBVTT

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.770
The one who opens this door gains
new power.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:25.920
But as compensation,
he will lose what’s most important to him.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.630
My most important?

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:39.810
Ouch...

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.020
I had that dream again.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.270
Oh no!

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.230
I’m late!

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.230
I’m late!

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.770
Desk, leave the front page open
for a 3 o’clock submission.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.300
I’m writing an excellent article!

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.450
Akari!

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.620
You could’ve woken me up!

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.040
I’m busy delivering the news
in the morning.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.560
Since you’re now in middle school,
you can wake up by yourself.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.210
I’m leaving!

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.270
Yuma, did you eat breakfast?

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.490
No time for that! I’m late!

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.560
What are you doing, Grandma?

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.360
Breakfast is the energy source
for the entire day.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.020
You must eat!

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:31.520
I understand!

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.150
Cleaning.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.580
Out of the way!

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:41.670
Cleaning!

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:42.370
Sorry!

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.740
Yuma!

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.210
Tetsuo!

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.540
I’ll race you to class!

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.500
You can’t beat me with that belly!

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.550
I’m kattobing!

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.180
Take that!

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.010
Cleaning!

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.570
Damn!

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:11.110
Cleaning.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.360
My deck!

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.820
Stop it!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:14.910
Garbage.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.780
My deck isn’t garbage!

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.530
Junk.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.990
It’s not a junk deck either!

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.740
You suck.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.230
You’re doing this on purpose!

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.380
Hey, Kotori.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.290
Isn’t that Yuma?

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.230
Who knows...

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.250
He’s such a fool.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:43.970
It’s impossible!

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.310
It’s impossible to jump over
twenty vaulting boxes!

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.190
I’ll make that height!

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.320
I’m kattobing!

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.940
Are you okay, Yuma?

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.390
I’m kattobing...

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.490
You idiot!

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.220
Do your best!

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.510
It’s impossible!

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:09.660
There’s no way he can make it!

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.360
I’ll make it without taking a breath!

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.170
I’m kattobing—

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:15.740
Yuma!

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:23.340
Basically, a sentence has a subject
and a predicate...

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.560
Sheesh, you’re such a fool.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.100
It’s a challenge.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.170
It’s kattobi...

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.370
It’s kattobing.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.480
But you didn’t succeed at all.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.780
Kotori, you don’t understand.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.460
What’s important is to keep kattobing!

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.530
As long as I don’t give up,
I might reach my goal someday.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:47.490
Besides, I have this key.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.460
That’s a memento from your
explorer parents, right?

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.100
Yeah!

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:56.990
This key opens the door to
lots of potential!

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.320
Does it really have that power?

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.260
Nope!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.010
It doesn’t?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.250
But when I have this key,
I feel like I can kattobing!

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.390
Kattobing!

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:18.570
And I kattobing the most when...

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:21.570
Here it is!

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.030
They’re doing it!

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.760
D-Gazer set!

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:50.780
I’m going to become
the dueling world champion!

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.730
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.860
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.910
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:10.030
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:17.420
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:24.100
I lied, thinking it was easier
to be alone

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:30.510
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:34.390
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.520
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.540
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.530
Everyone is not the same

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:47.610
That’s the reason for living

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:52.870
Even if the sounds are dissonant
at times

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:58.290
That’s why I never give up!
I believe my strength will get me through

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.370
I travel to the edge of the world

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:06.010
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.840
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard
or the scorching sun

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.390
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:15.480
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.600
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:32.630
I’m Kattobing!!

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:32.630
Number 1:

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:32.630
I’m Kattobing!!

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.320
Today, who will I—

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.580
Challenge to continue your record losing streak?

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.580
You’re lowering my excitement!

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.310
If I keep kattobing, the losing
streak will end someday!

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:41.540
Yuma, look!

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.500
It’s Tetsuo.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.450
Yuma, look at Tetsuo’s opponent.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:51.890
Shark!

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.430
Xyz Summon!

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:58.460
When there are two or more monsters
on the field with the same Level,

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:02.900
I can use those monsters as Material
to Special Summon an Xyz Monster!

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:08.180
I overlay Level 3 Skull Kraken
and Big Jaws!

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.260
Xyz Summon!

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:17.790
Come, Submersible Carrier Aero Shark!

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.420
Xyz Summon!

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.580
Yeah!

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:29.650
The most unique feature of Xyz Summoning
is that the Material Monsters don’t go to the graveyard.

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:33.690
They become Overlay Units
and support the Xyz Monster!

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:39.600
I don’t have a single Xyz Monster,
but they’re incredible!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.300
Go, Aero Shark!

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.440
Attack him directly!

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:56.620
Tetsuo...

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.370
As promised, I’m taking this.

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:03.270
What are you planning to do with
Tetsuo’s deck?

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.200
Who are you?

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.930
I’m Yuma Tsukumo!

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.300
I’m his classmate!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.800
Don’t you know who he is?

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:14.140
Yeah, I know.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.760
He’s notorious in this school.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:17.480
Shark!

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.270
How dare you say that.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.980
But I won this prize fair and square.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.090
What?

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:26.440
We bet our decks in this duel.

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:28.670
Why would you do that?

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:34.530
He said that I wasn’t skilled enough
to be called a duelist.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:39.990
Then I’ll defeat him in a duel
and get your deck back!

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.530
You idiot!

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:45.180
Shark’s skills are so good that
he appeared in the national tournament!

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.290
There’s no way you can beat him!

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.130
Don’t be so sure!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.460
Because my goal is to become
a dueling champion!

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.720
A dueling champion?

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.030
Do you know how hard it is to
become a dueling champion?

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:00.520
Well, no...

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:03.980
Then you better watch what you say!

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:07.110
I’m free to dream!

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.690
Dream...

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:14.150
If you want this deck back,
bet your most precious item.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:18.120
My most precious item?

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.070
What are you doing?

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:26.230
It seems this is really precious.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:26.920
Give it back!

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.420
I’ll show you how much this
is really worth.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:35.880
You learn how precious something
is when you lose it.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.340
You learn its true value!

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.310
How dare you!

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.980
Your precious item is broken.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.860
Now it’s gone!

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.780
Too bad, but I can’t give this deck back.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.020
That’s dirty, Shark!

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:01.780
Stop it!

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:04.230
But I’ll give you a chance.

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:08.250
If you’re going to talk about being the future dueling champion, let’s battle in a duel.

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:11.480
If you beat me, I’ll give back this deck.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:12.960
But if I win...

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:15.170
I get your deck!

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:19.360
Sunday at the courtyard in front
of the station.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.880
Go there if you want his deck back.

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:31.400
The one who opens this door
gains new power.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:37.360
But as compensation,
he will lose what’s most important to him.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:44.350
At this rate...

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:51.690
Yuma, you’re not going to try
for twenty today?

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.300
Not today.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.170
Yuma...

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:02.140
Yuma, aren’t you going to kattobing?

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.600
Maybe next time.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.560
Cheer up, Yuma!

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.100
I know.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:13.150
But I can’t muster up the strength.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:17.590
Since my key broke, I can’t kattobing.

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:18.610
Yuma...

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:27.310
Yuma!

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.590
Tetsuo!

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:33.500
Yuma, are you planning to duel tomorrow?

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.950
I guess...

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:36.960
Don’t go.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.650
You won’t succeed!

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:40.130
You don’t know that!

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:43.930
Since I couldn’t beat him,
there’s no way you can beat Shark!

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:47.770
Besides, it’s my fault to begin with.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.620
I don’t want to owe you.

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:53.500
Don’t get the wrong idea.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:56.520
I’m not going for you.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:00.030
He destroyed my precious item
in front of my eyes.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.700
And I’m supposed to back off?

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.200
My parents wouldn’t run away!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.080
I’m going to fight for myself!

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.070
Do whatever you like!

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:15.130
I’ll give you this.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:20.840
You searched for it?

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.550
I randomly found it!

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:32.520
How am I supposed to use this card?

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:36.270
My dad used this deck.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:40.200
If I can master it, it must be powerful.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.460
I’m leaving!

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:43.640
Yuma!

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.320
What is it, Grandma?

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:46.470
Here!

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:48.280
What’s this?

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:52.250
Take it. You can’t fight on
an empty stomach.

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.920
I applaud you for your fearlessness.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.090
But if you ran away, you could’ve
saved your deck.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:10.010
I’d rather quit dueling then
run away from you!

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.300
I have to do this!

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:15.060
I’m kattobing!

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:22.340
Duel Disk set!

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:27.450
D-Gazer set!

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.530
Duel target locked on!

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:40.760
AR Vision Link complete.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:41.750
Duel!

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:46.130
Do your best, Yuma!

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:48.590
Here I go! My turn!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.390
I draw!

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:54.640
The strongest monster in my hand is...

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.900
I summon Zubaba Knight!

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.400
Zubaba!

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:07.400
The first player can’t attack
on the first turn.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.660
I end my turn!

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:14.370
Your strongest card only has
1600 ATK?

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.330
My turn.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.120
I draw!

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:22.380
I summon Big Jaws!

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.800
1800 ATK!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.930
Zubaba Knight has 1600 ATK.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:37.280
Big Jaws has 1800.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:40.150
When monsters in attack position battle...

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:44.480
...the monster with lower ATK is destroyed, and the controller takes the difference as damage.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:47.530
You had a monster in your hand
that’s stronger than Zubaba Knight?

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:50.570
You should summon your weaklings
in defense position.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:56.040
But even if you had a stronger monster,
it would’ve been pointless.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.670
I activate the spell card Aqua Jet!

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:05.510
Until this turn’s End Phase,
a WATER monster gains 1000 ATK!

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:07.050
There it is!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.930
It’s Shark’s spell combo!

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:10.720
Battle!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.350
Go, Big Jaws!

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.100
Big Mouth!

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.060
Zubaba Sword!

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.990
Zubaba!

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:30.860
I set one card.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.030
I end my turn.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:33.830
Damn!

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:37.040
But I only lost 1200 LP!

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.790
My turn! I draw!

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.670
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.800
I’m counting on you, Gagaga Magician!

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:49.090
What?

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.760
You put it in attack position
when it only has 1500 ATK?

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:55.180
What a stupid mistake!

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.470
You’re wrong!

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:01.690
From my hand, I equip Wonder Wand
on Gagaga Magician!

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:06.820
The monster equipped with
Wonder Wand gains 500 ATK!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:12.320
If it has low ATK,
I’ll power it up with an Equip Spell!

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.780
Hooray! It now has more
ATK than Big Jaws!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.290
Go, Gagaga Magician!

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.160
Attack Big Jaws!

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:24.630
You’re not worried at all about
my set card?

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.710
I activate my trap!

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.050
A trap card?

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:30.760
Zeus’s Breath!

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:36.800
When your monster attacks,
this card negates that attack!

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:46.860
And when a WATER monster is on my field,
you take 800 points of damage.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:50.320
My Big Jaws is a WATER monster.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.700
Therefore, you take 800 points of damage.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.920
Damn...

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.170
I get it! A trap card!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.430
All right!

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:13.300
I set one trap card and end my turn!

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:17.640
Yuma, you can set two types of cards:
spells and traps.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.970
Don’t say which one out loud!

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.600
Play better!

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.020
You fool!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.810
My turn! I draw!

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.770
I summon Skull Kraken!

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.360
600 ATK.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.530
All right.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:41.330
He doesn’t have a monster with more
ATK than my Gagaga Magician!

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:44.000
Not so fast.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.920
I activate Skull Kraken’s effect!

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:54.550
When Skull Kraken is summoned, I can destroy one face-up spell or trap card on your field.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:57.300
I destroy Wonder Wand!

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.760
What?

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:02.770
Now Gagaga Magician has less ATK than Big Jaws.

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.390
This is bad!

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:07.480
Shark now has two monsters.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:10.440
They’re the same ones
from when he dueled me.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:13.820
He’s planning to Xyz Summon!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.400
Like I thought, Yuma doesn’t stand a chance.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.870
Yuma...

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:20.240
What’s wrong?

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:24.080
Did you really think you could become
a dueling champion with your lame skills?

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:26.580
It’s no good.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.750
Since my key is broken, I can’t kattobing.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.300
If only my key wasn’t broken...

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:36.550
You can’t win a duel because
you rely on that object!

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:37.510
What?

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.840
I have a good idea.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:44.720
Just like that key, when I get your deck,
I’ll rip it up in front of your eyes!

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.480
How dare you!

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:49.940
You can’t accomplish anything alone!

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:54.320
Whatever!

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.650
I’m not like that!

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:57.780
No matter how many times I fail...

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:58.950
No matter how many times I get laughed at...

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:04.790
I can keep kattobing because
I believe in myself!

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:09.160
My kattobing isn’t over yet!

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:19.680
The key...

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:22.800
Now open the door.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.520
This place is...

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:28.030
Open the door.

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:31.400
If you do, you will gain new power.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:37.280
But as compensation, you will lose
what’s most important to you.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:44.910
Super kattobing!

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:02.800
Ouch.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.300
What’s this?

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:13.060
Was that a dream?

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:15.730
No...

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:17.770
What’s going on?

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:22.280
I’m brimming with power!

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:27.160
Summon me. Summon the Number.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:34.000
I overlay Level 3 Big Jaws
and Skull Kraken!

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:42.840
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:49.890
Come, Number 17: Leviathan Dragon!

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.620
Number?

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.950
That’s not the monster
he summoned against me.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.370
Then what is it?

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:15.630
I don’t know.

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:17.670
I never heard of a Number.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:21.380
Leviathan Dragon’s effect activates!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:27.970
Once per turn, I can use an Overlay Unit
to increase Leviathan Dragon’s ATK by 500!

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:29.260
What?

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.770
Go, Leviathan Dragon!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.440
Vice Stream!

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:46.370
Yuma!

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:48.820
The match is over.

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.830
I’ll finish you with the next attack!

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:53.290
Ouch...

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:54.300
Damn.

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:55.290
I’m not good enough...

00:21:56.090 --> 00:21:56.540
Stand up.

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:02.510
We’ll win.

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:05.800
Who are you?

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:15.100
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:18.480
This week’s quiz:

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:21.330
There are three main types of cards!

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:24.320
Spells, traps and... What’s the last one?

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:34.830
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:39.880
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:54.430
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:59.480
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:01.900
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.780
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:07.200
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:08.820
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:13.620
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers
on that sheet

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:18.040
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:23.590
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:28.090
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:33.220
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:37.140
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:43.690
A weirdo suddenly appeared next to me.

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:45.440
What was his name again?

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:46.650
We’re going to win, idiot.

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:49.780
My name’s not idiot! It’s Yuma!

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:52.910
And he arrogantly orders me around
during the duel!

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:54.200
It’s my turn!

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:55.960
No, it’s my turn!

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:58.160
I don’t have time to deal with him!

00:23:58.160 --> 00:24:01.540
In my duel against Shark,
Tetsuo’s deck and mine are on the line!

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:04.000
I can’t afford to lose!

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:09.970
My Name is Astral

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:07.380
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“My Name is Astral”

00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:09.970
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:12.930
The answer is...

00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:15.180
Monster!

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:20.190
Powerful monsters are great
in a heated battle!

00:24:20.190 --> 00:24:24.980
I’m excited to see what monsters
will appear in the next episode!
